	)
	(text_box "SerDes\n\nWe use SD1 as XFI with a AQR113C PHY (as per LS1046A RDB)\nAQR113C/114C/115C pin compatible 10g/5g/2.5g PHY\n\n===============================\nLS1046 has two SerDes:\n( We duplicate the RDB board's config )\n\nSerDes1 lanes:\n- LANE 0: XFI 10gbit mac9 PLL2  (SFP+ cage)\n- LANE 1: XFI 10gbit mac10 PLL2 (SFP+ cage)\n- LANE 2: SGMII(1gbit) mac5 PLL1\n- LANE 3: SGMII(1gbit) mac6 PLL1\n\nSerDes2 lanes:\n- LANE 0: One mPCIE x1 PLL2\n- LANE 1: One PCIE x1 PLL2\n- LANE 2: One PCIE x1 PLL2\n- LANE 3: One SATA PLL1\n\n\nSerDes is powered down by disabling both PLLs of a SerDes\n\n==============================\nDPAA contains FMAN\n\nFman manages ethernet packets in hardware.\nIt has 10 MACs:\n- MAC 9 and 10 support XFI\n- Others: RGMII SGMII SGMII2.5\nIt has a Parse, Classify, Distribute module: PCD\n\nSecurity offload: SEC\n- Interface between Fman and SEC is through: QMan BMan\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.66 12.7 0)
		(size 83.82 76.2)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
